<title>USA: Kansas feedlot cattle market quiet, no sales - USDA.</title>
<headline>Kansas feedlot cattle market quiet, no sales - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>DODGE CITY 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Trade was quiet, with no sales slaughter steers or heifers confirmed, USDA said.</p>
<p>Inquiry fair, demand light. Sales confirmed for the week to date on 66,300 head including 26,000 head or about 39 percent previously contracted or formulated cattle. Bids $67.00, asking $68.00, last sales Wednesday at $68.00.</p>
<p>Sales FOB feedlot net weights after 4 percent shrink.</p>
<p>Confirmed - none</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312 408 8720))</p>
